    <!-- Welcome and the guide -->
    <string name="welcome_text">Every wish to buy goes into a bottle and ages. The ones that are still alive when they’re ripe, you open: no guilt, they passed the test of time. The ones that fade, you pour into the barrel of your real dream. No bank, no receipts, no internet: only what you bring down yourself.</string>
    <string name="how_it_works">How it works</string>
    <string name="go_down">Go down to the cellar</string>
    <string name="setup_title">Before you go down</string>
    <string name="setup_currency">Prices are written in:</string>
    <string name="setup_dream">What is the barrel for? The money of every poured wish flows into it. Optional.</string>
    <string name="setup_dream_later">You can chalk it on the barrel later.</string>
    <string name="sample_dream">Japan</string>
    <string name="g1_title">Lay it down</string>
    <string name="g1_text">Want to buy something? Don’t buy it yet: lay it in the cellar. Type it in, or press “Share” in any shop and pick Cellar. And say honestly why you want it right now.</string>
    <string name="g2_title">Let it age</string>
    <string name="g2_text">The price picks the bottle: a vial ages three days, a bottle two weeks, a magnum a month, a cask three months; you can change the prices and the ageing in the settings. Dust settles, a cobweb grows, the label yellows. Time does its work.</string>
    <string name="g3_title">The tasting</string>
    <string name="g3_text">When a bottle is ripe, go down and take it in your hands. Still want it? Open it, that is, buy it, without a scrap of guilt. Faded? Pour it out. Not sure? Another week on the rack.</string>
    <string name="g4_title">The dream’s barrel</string>
    <string name="g4_text">What you pour out doesn’t vanish: it flows into the barrel of your real dream, a trip, a safety cushion, a bicycle. Saying no to one thing becomes getting closer to another.</string>
    <string name="g5_title">The journal and the ledger</string>
    <string name="g5_text">A month after opening, the sommelier asks: still a joy, so-so, or vinegar? The ledger shows which reasons bring vinegar and which wishes fade. And on 11.11 and Black Friday there’s a storm above: whatever is laid then ages twice as long.</string>

